# Build and tooling output
# Everything a build, a test run or a tooling script produces goes under `output/`. Both build systems now
# refuse a build directory that lands inside the tree anywhere else, but each writes something before its
# guard runs - qbs creates the directory it was pointed at, CMake writes its cache before it reads
# CMakeLists.txt - so the names they fall back to stay ignored: qbs names its build directory after the
# configuration, CMake writes wherever `-B` points.
/output/
CMakeUserPresets.json
/CMakeCache.txt
/CMakeFiles/
/build/
/default/
/debug/
/release/
/profiling/
/staging/
/consumer/

# Other
*.user
*.spv
.vscode
